ef 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1050 1320.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096910 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "acc24286-334e-50b7-b51f-39796fa9c946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1061 618388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e5d3fd98-fbd8-5b6d-a250-876573acf24e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097774 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1061 618389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "333f87c0-71a4-538e-9783-f364abf0caa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1061 618392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdfdcd42-ada8-5eea-ae27-e68cd87d7470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1061 618395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0d6168f-5f91-5b54-9679-17a077751add" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{′}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1065 897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dbf22d18-c638-527f-a085-8fcc19fbfbeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100455 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "09aa265b-d358-5ee1-8520-4f4d7c406505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100467 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17