}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(0,-2),(2,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401015 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4d94100e-63ab-58cf-b2c0-0f485eafe140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401016 #edb/ref 1080 "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+16{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401016 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401016 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c77b2f36-6be8-50c0-ae22-868fa6cf86a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401017 #edb/ref 1080 "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\